<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhu</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Moon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhu is an island in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a>, between Saaremaa and the mainland, and the third largest in the country. Its people resisted the German crusaders until 1227, when the island was taken in the conquest of Saaremaa. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was held by the Livonian Order. Its villages preserve traditional thatched farmhouses and a distinctive folk dress.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/muhu.jpg" alt="Muhu" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hiiumaamudeliklubi · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Koguva_sadam_2015.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
